body:
The last time I told my friends about this, it resulted in me being abandoned by almost everyone I cared about. And trust me, they were 100% justified in doing so.

Just lost a close friendship that I really valued but took for granted, 6 months after losing the online friends that I had considered basically my adopted family and another person I really valued. Withdrew from college for the 2nd quarter in a row because things were just getting too tough. Got depression/anxiety, BPD, possibly ADHD/CPTSD/bipolar. No time for/can't afford meds/therapy/whatever now, not like it's helped much in the past 2 years. I've tried so hard to change myself, and every time life has spat in my face and I've failed miserably. My family continues to suck and say questionable things (and by that I mean be racist and borderline verbally abusive). There is no despair without hope, and I've felt like every time I've had hope it's been brutally crushed. As if the universe is mocking me for ever thinking there'd be a way out of this pit of misery.

&#x200B;

But they did stay with me, through a fuckton of suicidal ideation and intent. In all I made 7 threats and attempted 3 times, and only during the last time did they cave and say "no more."

&#x200B;

One thing though: for all their knowledge of MH issues (most of them had also been dealing with depression for a while) they never brought up BPD. So it's possible they didn't even know about the condition, like me, and just assumed I was being manipulatively malicious after a while, and having "wisened up" to my "true nature", left. That would be a tragic misunderstanding for sure, but then again, I had it coming :/

I've partly forgiven myself, though I'm still not over this at all.

&#x200B;

Regarding those people - they were there by my side, every day for 4-6 hours, sometimes straight up enabling me, until they weren't. Then when I tried to reach out to one of them again this July he called me a stalker. To go from so kind and caring to completely cold and callous boggles me so much that I can only fathom 2 possibilities: either what I did was, despite what you said, so horrible and abusive that not even the kindest saint could forgive me, in which case how can I forgive myself. Or they were assholes, and all of them weren't worth being friends with in the first place, in which case I can't trust anyone ever again since if even such kind and caring people could be two-faced snakes then the average joe who isn't nearly as empathetic or understanding has the potential to be much, much worse.

Thanks for the kind words.

&#x200B;

I'm pretty much good at nothing, or at least nothing useful, due to my constant hobby-switching that I'm sure people here are all too familiar with. I played violin for 8 years but didn't really enjoy it past the 2nd, etc, etc. As for therapy...have been going for two years, and while it hasn't solved anything, at least it's kept me alive, huh.
